      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "The fire inspector continues his strict check and rejects several fire extinguishers. The restaurant owner, Dmitry, arrives and demands to know the real reason behind this sudden and aggressive inspection. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Где ваш огнетушитель?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Он висел здесь в прошлый раз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы что, смеётесь надо мной?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Этот не подходит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вот нормальный огнетушитель.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А где его пломба?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Добрый день.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Можно узнать одну вещь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Почему у вас такой интерес к ресторану?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы боремся с плохим руководством.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Был звонок моему начальнику.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Из соседнего ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Всё понятно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну что, до завтра.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Где ваш огнетушитель?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Where is your fire extinguisher?' — Notice the adverb meaning 'where' paired with the det for 'your'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Он висел здесь в прошлый раз.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It was hanging here last time.' — Notice the pronoun meaning 'he' paired with the verb for 'to hang, be hanging'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Вы что, смеётесь надо мной?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Are you laughing at me?' — Notice the pronoun meaning 'you' paired with the pronoun for 'what'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Этот не подходит.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This one is not suitable.' — Notice the det meaning 'this' paired with the verb for 'is coming up, is approaching'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вот нормальный огнетушитель.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here is a normal fire extinguisher.' — Notice the adjective meaning 'decent, normal' paired with the noun for 'fire extinguisher'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А где его пломба?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And where is its seal?' — Notice the adverb meaning 'where' paired with the pronoun for 'him'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Добрый день.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Good afternoon.' — Notice the adjective meaning 'good' paired with the noun for 'day'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Можно узнать одну вещь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'May I know one thing?' — Notice the adverb meaning 'may, can' paired with the verb for 'to find out'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Почему у вас такой интерес к ресторану?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why do you have such an interest in the restaurant?' — Notice the adverb meaning 'why' paired with the pronoun for 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы боремся с плохим руководством.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We are fighting with bad management.' — Notice the pronoun meaning 'we' paired with the verb for 'to fight, struggle'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Был звонок моему начальнику.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'There was a call to my boss.' — Notice the verb meaning 'was' paired with the noun for 'call; bell'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Из соседнего ресторана.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'From the neighboring restaurant.' — Notice the adjective meaning 'neighboring' paired with the noun for 'restaurant'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "guest",
      "t": "Всё понятно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everything is clear.' — Notice the det meaning 'everything' paired with the adverb for '(is) clear'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ну что, до завтра.",
      "gap": 0.55
